# This project is developed on Windows and deployed to Linux containers.
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise hand Docker a CRLF copy of the entrypoint,
# and the kernel then reads its shebang as "/bin/sh\r" -- the container exits
# with "no such file or directory" and names a file that is plainly there.
# Anything the Linux image executes or parses is pinned to LF.
* text=auto

*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.toml        text eol=lf
*.sql         text eol=lf
.env.example  text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
